{
  "name": "Searing Sunburst",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You gain the ability to create an orb of light that erupts into a devastating explosion. As an Action, you magically create an orb and hurl it at a point you choose within 150 feet, where it erupts into a sphere of radiant light for a brief but deadly instant.</p><p>Each creature in that 20-foot-radius sphere must succeed on a Constitution Saving Throw or take 2d6 radiant damage. A creature doesn't need to make the save if the creature is behind total cover that is opaque.</p><p>You can increase the sphere's damage by spending ki points. Each point you spend, to a maximum of 3, increases the damage by 2d6.</p>",
